WEBVTT

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:06.860
Yokohama

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:06.860
Shopping Trip Log

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:14.770
Gone shopping
in Yokohama

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:35.280
Some years ago,

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:36.900
the owner…

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:39.450
entrusted me with the shop

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:41.530
and went away somewhere.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:56.770
Where to? What for?

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.590
Will he return someday?

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:09.840
I think it’s good that I’m a robot.

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:14.020
No matter how long it takes, I can wait.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:27.860
Gone shopping
in Yokohama

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:27.860
To Alpha
I’m glad to see you are doing well.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:49.210
Morning
February 2nd

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:16.440
Coffee – I seem to end up drinking eight-tenths of it myself.

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:21.110
Have ya arranged a ride back?

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:21.980
I have.

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:24.240
I’d really like to take you all the way,

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:26.100
but someone is waiting for me.

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:28.620
Not at all. You have been a great help to me.

00:04:30.110 --> 00:04:30.870
Sorry.

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:16.770
…and follow that road to the end,
and ya’ll be there.

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:18.520
Thank you.

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:24.320
I’d love to give ya a ride, but the gasoline truck will be here soon.

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:26.970
Please don’t worry about it.
It sounds near enough.

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:28.350
Sorry.

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:37.650
She looks familiar.

00:05:57.150 --> 00:05:58.040
Hatsuseno.

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:02.560
The front door?

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:07.300
Coming!

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:11.100
Who might you be?

00:06:12.230 --> 00:06:14.310
Are you Hatsuseno Alpha-san?

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:16.520
Huh? Oh yeah, that’s right.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:20.140
It’s been so long since anyone has called me by my full name. I had to think for a second.

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:25.100
I’m from the Musashino Express Delivery Service.

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:26.560
Uh, express delivery?

00:06:27.230 --> 00:06:29.350
I haven’t received a package in a long time!

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:30.430
Who is it from?

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:32.120
Let me see.

00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:35.080
It’s from a Mr. Hatsuseno.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:46.310
I know you’re busy, but thanks for the company.

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:48.680
Not at all. Besides, I’ve…

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:49.970
Ah, gee, I wonder what it is.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:52.930
I don’t mind whatever it is though.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:03.770
Is this a camera?

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:05.010
It seems to be…

00:07:05.010 --> 00:07:07.860
Oh gosh… but why a camera?

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.260
Such an odd person, you know.

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:13.010
Do you know anything about it?

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:19.650
I do have a message from the sender to give to you.

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:21.180
You do? May I?

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:25.560
No, it’s a direct message.

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:26.900
Eh? Direct?

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:27.310
Yes.

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:28.630
A direct message?

00:07:29.690 --> 00:07:34.390
Um, excuse my rudeness, but…
you are a type A7M2, right?

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:36.930
A7…?

00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:41.350
Ah, I remember having a name like that too.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:43.520
Directly?

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:44.100
That’s right.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:47.520
Does that mean you’re a…

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:51.470
No, I’m a more common model – type A7M3.

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:55.570
Eh?! You’re a robot?!

00:07:56.860 --> 00:07:59.100
What? You didn’t realize?

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:09.010
I’ll transfer the message directly, then.

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:11.640
Umm… can’t you just tell me?

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:15.190
Well, I don’t know the details myself.

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:17.430
Besides, it shouldn’t take too long.

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:19.470
Let’s do it. Hold my hands.

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:21.260
Please show me your tongue.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:24.140
Are you ready?

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:29.980
Please don’t shy away.

00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:31.820
Well then, excuse me.

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:00.260
Did you receive it?

00:09:00.730 --> 00:09:02.140
I’ll need a moment…

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:10.440
The message from the owner felt something like this:

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:14.180
“I don’t think I will be coming home for some time.”

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:19.640
“Do not worry about it. I encourage you to go out and see the world around you.”

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:26.510
“Ten years or a single day may not make a difference to you right now.”

00:09:27.270 --> 00:09:30.890
“But someday, there might be things you may like to be nostalgic about.”

00:09:32.190 --> 00:09:34.850
“In hope that it will assist you in capturing such moments more vividly,

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:36.370
I send this camera to you.”

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:39.890
“Take good care,” it said.

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:46.060
Why, I feel nostalgic already.

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:09.640
Sorry for making you drive me back.

00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:13.340
I can’t believe you were about to walk ten kilometers to the station.

00:10:17.770 --> 00:10:20.800
Have them come to my
house next time, okay?

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:21.640
I will.

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:33.430
Hi there, Ojisan!

00:10:33.430 --> 00:10:35.810
Oh, how are ya?

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:59.100
Musashino, huh? That’s pretty far.

00:10:59.770 --> 00:11:01.220
It’s not really that far.

00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:06.600
I wonder when they’ll get here.

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:08.850
It happens all the time.

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:11.650
Besides, we got here
a little bit early, so…

00:11:21.980 --> 00:11:24.350
Kokone? That’s a cute name.

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:35.350
When I first visited the training institute,
I made up that name myself.

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:44.850
I forgot why I named myself that.

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:49.850
Um, may I ask what your model name is, Alpha?

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:53.140
Alpha is my model name.

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:57.850
I was born when the Alpha-type models were still rare…

00:12:02.060 --> 00:12:04.510
so I was simply referred to as “Alpha,”

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:06.810
and it became my actual name.

00:12:10.270 --> 00:12:11.870
Well, I kind of like it too, so…

00:12:12.220 --> 00:12:14.000
Ah, as I thought.

00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:22.010
Oh yeah, about this camera.

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:25.050
Oh, you brought it with you?

00:12:25.310 --> 00:12:27.810
Mmm-hmm. Can you tell me how to operate it?

00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:29.640
Can I take a look at it?

00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:35.260
Yeah. For these models…

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:39.760
you usually take one of these caramel-like capsules…

00:12:43.230 --> 00:12:45.060
open the back cover like this…

00:12:47.520 --> 00:12:49.260
insert it in the hole…

00:12:50.650 --> 00:12:52.220
and close the cover.

00:12:52.690 --> 00:12:56.060
Then, you push the lid of the lens here and press this.

00:12:58.690 --> 00:13:01.920
One piece should be good
for three hundred pictures.

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:23.070
You know, about this lens…

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:26.640
It seems they are made of the same things as our eyes.

00:13:26.940 --> 00:13:29.560
So it is an eyeball after all.

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:32.110
Do you have a cord?

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:35.120
Hmm… Oh, this?

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:36.160
Yes.

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:39.760
Plug the thin end of the cord into the hole in the cap.

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:41.530
Plug it in, and…

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:44.170
If you put the other end into your mouth…

00:13:48.110 --> 00:13:50.430
you can see what the camera sees.

00:13:50.770 --> 00:13:51.600
This feels…

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:53.560
kinda awkward.

00:13:54.150 --> 00:13:58.100
It is rather neat to be able to see yourself with your eyes closed, isn’t it?

00:14:16.310 --> 00:14:18.970
Mmm, I think I get it now.

00:14:19.480 --> 00:14:20.560
Say “cheese”!

00:14:27.650 --> 00:14:32.550
Afternoon
January 1st

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:35.850
A while later, her ride arrived.

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:41.970
Would it be okay if I visited sometime outside of work?

00:14:41.970 --> 00:14:43.470
Of course! Visit anytime.

00:14:47.230 --> 00:14:48.510
Thank you for everything.

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:02.430
I think we will meet again.

00:15:06.150 --> 00:15:09.510
Looking at her going back to an unknown world…

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:13.550
it feels lonely, but…

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:17.930
Musashino county.

00:15:19.860 --> 00:15:21.650
Once known…

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:24.520
as the Capital of the East.

00:15:41.110 --> 00:15:42.960
Although it’s only a neighboring county,

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:45.790
it feels further away…

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:47.340
than it actually is.

00:16:17.060 --> 00:16:20.830
Ojisan—!

00:16:22.610 --> 00:16:23.330
Huh?

00:16:25.860 --> 00:16:27.180
What’cha want?

00:16:28.940 --> 00:16:29.940
Need gas?

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:33.180
Nope. I’m sorry for waking you up though.

00:16:36.810 --> 00:16:39.060
D’ya know that girl?

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:42.060
She asked me for directions this afternoon.

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:46.260
By the way, she looks a lot like you.

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:50.010
I was kinda surprised, just a little.

00:16:51.020 --> 00:16:51.900
She looks like me?

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:52.900
Yep.

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:55.510
She’s my little sister.

00:17:10.980 --> 00:17:14.170
There isn’t a single superfluous scene.

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:32.930
Three hundred shots are not nearly enough.

00:17:54.360 --> 00:18:02.260
The sky is blanketed in bright red…

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:10.240
when the tilted sunset changes its face.

00:18:10.850 --> 00:18:18.930
Look closely…

00:18:19.520 --> 00:18:27.140
at the whispering lullaby of the waves.

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:31.390
The light flickers…

00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:35.770
from afar in my heart.

00:18:35.770 --> 00:18:43.720
I let myself drift in the direction of my memories,

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:51.850
to the town I once visited, far, far away.

00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:23.260
The owner sent me a camera a little while ago.

00:19:24.810 --> 00:19:27.010
I’ve carefully put it away since then.

00:19:32.610 --> 00:19:35.430
I know I should be using it more often.

00:19:36.650 --> 00:19:41.100
After all, it’s light and perfect to carry around as an accessory.

00:20:27.980 --> 00:20:29.330
It was made for my gun.

00:20:30.230 --> 00:20:31.930
It’s a little big, but…

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:37.000
It’s perfect!

00:20:40.650 --> 00:20:42.510
All right! Today, I will take some pictures!

00:21:07.810 --> 00:21:10.260
My, don’t you look handsome?

00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:18.720
At a closer look…

00:21:19.730 --> 00:21:22.850
there are so many scenes to photograph.

00:21:44.810 --> 00:21:45.850
Not yet.

00:22:05.230 --> 00:22:08.590
Ojisan—!

00:22:10.480 --> 00:22:12.390
Oh, what brings ya here?

00:22:13.860 --> 00:22:16.810
I want you to model a bit for me. Is that all right?

00:22:17.190 --> 00:22:18.350
Huh?

00:22:22.560 --> 00:22:24.440
Just be casual.

00:22:25.690 --> 00:22:27.510
Try to act natural.

00:22:53.440 --> 00:22:55.180
I… I’m sorry!

00:22:56.190 --> 00:22:57.230
Mmm, what’s that about?

00:22:57.770 --> 00:22:59.060
I’ll be back again.

00:23:03.110 --> 00:23:05.280
This is not going well.

00:23:19.410 --> 00:23:20.640
All right.

00:23:28.480 --> 00:23:30.180
Maybe I should try a nearer scene.

00:23:57.690 --> 00:24:00.560
There are still hundreds of pictures left;

00:24:00.940 --> 00:24:02.930
one or two should not matter.

00:24:04.690 --> 00:24:07.810
When did I become so stingy?

00:24:19.150 --> 00:24:20.890
There are many wonderful scenes,

00:24:22.400 --> 00:24:23.100
but…

00:24:24.100 --> 00:24:26.140
I am really after one picture.

00:24:27.690 --> 00:24:29.600
I was really after that one picture.

00:24:54.310 --> 00:24:55.640
The northern ruins.

00:24:56.770 --> 00:24:58.600
I decided that I would take that picture at sunset.

00:25:01.980 --> 00:25:03.600
The silhouette of Eno Island,

00:25:04.850 --> 00:25:06.430
and the street lights lined up above the water.

00:25:10.230 --> 00:25:11.860
In an instant…

00:25:12.900 --> 00:25:14.550
the sky turns wisteria purple.

00:26:08.020 --> 00:26:14.420
Navigation

00:26:16.480 --> 00:26:20.550
Entranced by the scenery,

00:26:21.100 --> 00:26:22.970
I was unable to take a picture.

00:26:24.730 --> 00:26:25.930
I couldn’t push the shutter.

00:26:31.730 --> 00:26:35.050
I ended up just carrying the camera all day.

00:26:45.310 --> 00:26:48.510
The picture of my scooter I took on the way out…

00:26:49.730 --> 00:26:51.350
was the only picture of the day.

00:26:54.940 --> 00:26:59.260
But that one picture… is good enough for me.

00:27:05.310 --> 00:27:09.680
The number of pictures remaining is not so meager after all.

00:27:12.100 --> 00:27:17.890
Also, I can recall the scenery I’ve seen today in finer detail than usual.

00:27:20.520 --> 00:27:24.140
The moment… returns to me.

00:27:44.940 --> 00:27:47.140
The festival-like world…

00:27:47.850 --> 00:27:51.430
has slowly settled to a leisurely pace.

00:27:55.770 --> 00:27:57.300
To think that an era…

00:27:58.100 --> 00:28:01.350
would reach its twilight so pleasantly.

00:28:05.440 --> 00:28:10.260
The dangerous times have since been called the “Age of Evening Calm.”

00:28:25.770 --> 00:28:33.850
I will probably keep watching this twilight world… as long as time flows.
